      "quote_wikipedia": "Antoine Lavoisier is credited as the first to blow oxygen —of which he was co-discoverer—through a blowpipe to support the combustion of charcoal, in 1782. Others, such as Edward Daniel Clarke, employed hydrogen, and later mixed hydrogen and oxygen in the oxy-hydrogen blowpipe."
